<title>USA: Prime Service Inc Q4 pro forma shr rises.</title>
<headline>Prime Service Inc Q4 pro forma shr rises.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.24		    $0.11</p>
<p> Net			  6,700		    3,100</p>
<p> Revs			86,993		   64,551</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  25,822		   18,367</p>
<p>	  12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr			  $1.04		    $0.71</p>
<p> Net			 29,200		   19,900</p>
<p> Revs		     326,588		  242,787</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  21,743		   18,367</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE - Results are pro forma to assume the company's initial public offering had been completed at the beginning of the 1995 fiscal year. Pro forma results exclude extraordinary, non-recurring and other charges.</p>
<p>In Q4 1996, the company posted a net loss of $3.96 million, or $0.15 per share, versus a net loss of $4.46 million, or $0.24, including an extraordinary charge of $4.9 million, or $0.19.</p>
<p>For the full year, net income was $2 million, or $0.09 per share, compared with a net loss of $8.66 million, or $0.47 per share.</p>
<p>((-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
</text>
